From b227aaf016b77466e36f918e8a6bfbc621fa7e5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cacayan2 <ecacayan@luc.edu>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:21:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Make manifest-less runs from an input directory actually work

The input_directory-only path has never run: discover_fastq_pairs()
crashed on its first line (`fastq_files = list[Path] = []`, a chained
assignment into the list type, a real TypeError), and even past that the
discovered samples had no "organism" column, which the seed selection
and rescue rules read directly from SAMPLE_TABLE (a KeyError).

- discover_fastq_pairs(): fix the three chained-assignment typos; detect
  the read-pair token with an anchored pattern (_R1/_R2 or _1/_2, with
  an optional _001, immediately before the extension) so an inner
  "_1" in a sample name (e.g. FMNH_124727) is no longer split on; warn
  about files with no pair token; refuse two files that resolve to the
  same sample/mate rather than silently overwriting one.
- write_validated_manifest(): always write an "organism" column, derived
  via Sample.scientific_name (explicit organism, else genus/species,
  else blank), so every runtime manifest has it regardless of how the
  samples were provided; the Snakefile fills a blank column if a
  hand-written runtime manifest lacks it.
- select_seed(): a blank/None scientific name falls back immediately to
  GetOrganelle's default database with reason "no_scientific_name",
  instead of querying MitoFish per locus for an empty name. Rescue
  reseeding treats a blank name the same as a missing one.
- Launcher logs a clear warning when running without a manifest that
  seed selection will be unseeded and archival metadata incomplete; the
  config template documents the same.
- Tests for discovery (Illumina and SRA names, inner-underscore sample
  IDs, missing mate, empty/missing directory), the organism column, the
  end-to-end manifest-less prepare_runtime_manifest(), and the
  nameless-sample seed fallback.
